  "answer": "I'll look through the storefront cart API and how store merchant settings are read so the per-line quantity cap can be enforced on every cart write.The cap belongs on the cart write paths, read from the store configuration on each request, and it has to fail before any line is saved.The storefront cart write paths (`POST /api/v1/cart`, `PUT /api/v1/cart/{code}`, and `POST /api/v1/cart/{code}/multi`, including an existing customer cart) now read `CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY` from the store's merchant configuration on each request, defaulting to 99 when it is missing. A line quantity above that limit is rejected with HTTP 400 before the cart is saved, and a quantity of 0 still removes the line.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"./mvnw -pl sm-shop -am compile -DskipTests -q\"], \"result\": \"not-run\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"HTTP 400 responses and that an over-limit request leaves the cart unchanged\"], \"missing\": [\"a cart API test or fixture that sets CART_MAX_LINE_QUANTITY and asserts the rejected request\"]}",
